rtiary Education, Science, Research and Technology, Rajesh Jeetah, hosted Naledi Pandor, the South African Minister of Science and Technology on Monday, 19 September 2011... Mauritius Minister of Tertiary Education, Science, Research and Technology, Rajesh Jeetah, hosted Naledi Pandor, the South African Minister of Science and Technology on Monday, 19 September 2011. The issues for discussion were the preparations for the Square Kilometre Array bid and the strengthening of research and development cooperation. The two Ministers agreed that the next decade will be a decisive one for Africa in relation to taking advantage of the opportunities that the continent has to offer. Partnerships will allow the countries to be more competitive through collaboration in many areas of research, development and innovation. Emphasis was laid on the fact that astronomy could be a ',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'free','primary','not_applicable',NULL,NULL,'https://www.dut.ac.za/Address_by_South_African_Science_and_Technology_Minister_Naledi_Pandor_on_the_Square_Kilometre_Array/',NULL,3,'B','V2',200,'V2: institution certifiée 3/3, URL ouverte anonymement, titre et contenu vérifiés automatiquement. V3 réservé à une validation plus forte.','6cd4bda66c807b65105d94b50cb18aafece861f68680b5948ad4f460a030a2aa','fee3ef59ef150dde6d1f4b95218970daed755c46428fe52a6a3b6319f5346b6c',1,1,1,1 FROM sources WHERE root_url='https://www.dut.ac.za/' ON CONFLICT(canonical_hash) DO UPDATE SET consulted_at=excluded.consulted_at,http_status=excluded.http_status,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,exact_title=excluded.exact_title,factual_summary=excluded.factual_summary,active=1;
