ms leading to the progressive improvement of compre','Over 500 traditional health practitioners (THPs) are set to graduate tomorrow in a (graduation) ceremony hosted by the University and the KwaZulu-Natal Health Department. The graduation will begin tomorrow (8 July 2014) at the Osizweni Community Hall in Newcastle with the Tentative Programme Stakeholder’s Meeting. On Thursday and Friday (10-11 July 2014), the official graduation ceremonies will take place at the Edumbe Municipal Hall and at the Belgrade Community Hall (Pongola) respectively. The graduation comes after the University Research Co. LLC (URC) funded project trained 520 Traditional Health Practitioners. The project came shortly after South Africa adopted a policy of Primary Health Care Re-engineering. The policy states that primary healthcare should be sustained by integrated, functional and mutually supportive referral systems leading to the progressive improvement of compre',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'free','primary','not_applicable',NULL,NULL,'https://www.dut.ac.za/Programme_Seeking_To_Increase_Capacity_of_Traditional_Health_Practitioners_In_Supporting_the_Management_of_HIV_AIDS_STIs_and_TB_Bears_Fruit/',NULL,3,'B','V2',200,'V2: institution certifiée 3/3, URL ouverte anonymement, titre et contenu vérifiés automatiquement. V3 réservé à une validation plus forte.','4e52f53da879409acc61ca6be4abeffee9e106a7e7ef4dca688eea0e5053e2c4','7003dcf1078ee47332d143577bab6b711c8a87800f6a3906b028a85fd77ab10f',1,1,1,1 FROM sources WHERE root_url='https://www.dut.ac.za/' ON CONFLICT(canonical_hash) DO UPDATE SET consulted_at=excluded.consulted_at,http_status=excluded.http_status,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,exact_title=excluded.exact_title,factual_summary=excluded.factual_summary,active=1;
