tigious 2026 Millennium Fellowship, joining a global network of young leaders committed to advancing the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) through community-driven action.Presented by the United Nations Academic Impact (UNAI) and the Millennium Campus Network (MCN), the fellowship equips students with leadership, partnership-building, and project management skills while supporting initiatives that address some of the world’s most pressing challenges.Their selection places the UFS among more than 330 campuses across 60 countries chosen to host the programme in 2026. From more than 76 000 applications submitted worldwide, only about 5 500 students were selected as Millennium fellows, making the achievement particularly significant for the University and its student leaders. Turning ideas into im',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'free','primary','not_applicable',NULL,NULL,'https://www.ufs.ac.za/templates/news-archive/campus-news/2026/september/ufs-students-join-global-movement-for-sustainable-change-as-millennium-fellows',NULL,1,'B','V2',200,'V2: institution certifiée 3/3, URL ouverte anonymement, titre et contenu vérifiés automatiquement. V3 réservé à une validation plus forte.','d95ab65e3234076bff2c6b7c3f2c59f671f01d4a832538196a572233a9591652','13c8f173b074302d3452d484f11271bf5e0e789a6dfdf8d8ed8fa5d2f1a00a6c',1,1,1,1 FROM sources WHERE root_url='https://www.ufs.ac.za/' ON CONFLICT(canonical_hash) DO UPDATE SET consulted_at=excluded.consulted_at,http_status=excluded.http_status,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,exact_title=excluded.exact_title,factual_summary=excluded.factual_summary,active=1;
