ISR) is focused on Air Force, Space Force, DOD and Intelligence Community&rsquo;s scientific, technical and operational activities through graduate research programs. CTISR brings together cleared faculty across academic departments to solve difficult, multi-disciplinary technical intelligence problems. Several current research projects include: signature measurement; phenomenological understanding; algorithm development for target detection and tracking; battle space combustion characterization; event classification; material identification; dim target detection and tracking; sensor data fusion for TI enhancement; and understanding target signature phenomenology and remote sensing platforms for enhanced exploitation of intelligence data. CTISR is also spearheading a business model which will enable defense contractors an',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'free','primary','not_applicable',NULL,NULL,'https://www.afit.edu/CTISR/',NULL,2,'B','V2',200,'V2: institution certifiée 3/3, URL ouverte anonymement, titre et contenu vérifiés automatiquement. V3 réservé à une validation plus forte.','06004bafe693f76c6876ad5cb6595d36370d0d8c1c6a4d944d3080b632d95e62','c0bd18a199eba83e1b64bb617577d9d069b5e34ea6dd5cc16e36d0bb43cedff7',1,1,1,1 FROM sources WHERE root_url='https://www.afit.edu/' ON CONFLICT(canonical_hash) DO UPDATE SET consulted_at=excluded.consulted_at,http_status=excluded.http_status,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,exact_title=excluded.exact_title,factual_summary=excluded.factual_summary,active=1;
